        <Title>Global Satellite Shortwave Imagery</Title>
        <Abstract>The NOAA/NESDIS Global Mosaic of Geostationary Satellite Imagery (GMGSI) shortwave, mid-infrared band (~3.8 μm), has an hourly update frequency, approximately 3 km spatial resolution, and can be used to identify fog and low clouds at night, identify fire hot spots, detect volcanic ash, estimate sea-surface temperatures, and discriminate between ice crystal sizes during the day. Low-level atmospheric vector winds can be estimated with this band, and the band can be used to study urban heat islands.</Abstract>
