        <Name>global_water_vapor_imagery_mosaic</Name>
        <Title>Global Satellite Water Vapor Imagery</Title>
        <Abstract>The NOAA/NESDIS Global Mosaic of Geostationary Satellite Imagery (GMGSI) water vapor band (~6.7 µm), has an hourly update frequency, approximately 3 km spatial resolution, the data latency is two to three hours, and indicates the amount of water vapor contained in the mid to upper levels of the troposphere, with the darker grays indicating drier air and the brighter grays/whites indicating more saturated air. The upper-level water vapor band is used for tracking upper-tropospheric winds, identifying jet streams, forecasting hurricane track and mid-latitude storm motion, monitoring severe weather potential, estimating upper/mid-level moisture and identifying regions where the potential for turbulence exists.</Abstract>
