        <Title>GOES East &amp; West Satellite Shortwave Imagery</Title>
        <Abstract>NOAA/NASA Geostationary Operational Environmental Satellites (GOES) Shortwave Band 7 (3.9 μm), has a 5 min update frequency, 2 km spatial resolution, and can be used to identify fog and low clouds at night, identify fire hot spots, detect volcanic ash, estimate sea-surface temperatures, and discriminate between ice crystal sizes during the day. Low-level atmospheric vector winds can be estimated with this band, and the band can be used to study urban heat islands. The 3.9 μm is unique among ABI bands because it senses both emitted terrestrial radiation as well as significant reflected solar radiation during the day. This composite shortwave imagery contains GOES-19 (East) and GOES-18 (West) from GOES Advanced Baseline Imager (ABI) Level 1b (L1b), L1b products are calibrated and, where applicable, geographically corrected.</Abstract>
