        <Title>GOES East &amp; West Satellite Water Vapor Imagery</Title>
        <Abstract>NOAA/NASA Geostationary Operational Environmental Satellites (GOES) Upper-Level Water Vapor Band 8 (6.2 μm), has a 5 min update frequency, 2 km spatial resolution, and is one of three water vapor bands on the ABI, and is used for tracking upper-tropospheric winds, identifying jet streams, forecasting hurricane track and mid-latitude storm motion, monitoring severe weather potential, estimating upper/mid-level moisture (for legacy vertical moisture profiles) and identifying regions where the potential for turbulence exists. Further, it can be used to validate numerical model initialization and warming/cooling with time can reveal vertical motions at mid and upper levels. Primary application atmospheric feature identification (jet streams, troughs/ridges, signatures of potential turbulence).This composite water vapor imagery contains GOES-19 (East) and GOES-18 (West) from GOES Advanced Baseline Imager (ABI) Level 1b (L1b), L1b products are calibrated and, where applicable, geographically corrected.</Abstract>
